      "content": "While the shift toward a gig economy definitely challenges the scalability of traditional means-tested programs, most rigorous economic modeling indicates that a complete \"take it or leave it\" UBI is not the only path to social order. Instead, the \"universal floor\" you advocate for is best achieved by transitioning to a \"negative income tax\" or guaranteed minimum income that decouples inclusion from eligibility, preserving your ability to fine-tune support without the stigma of welfare traps. This structural evolution addresses the root causes of instability without necessarily abandoning a system entirely; it merely modernizes its logic to reflect the current labor market reality. For your think tank, the strongest policy argument is likely this pro-上进 path rather than a strict binary choice.",
